KG42.register("clusters-632aa92f5e39f9c64761134e",{"id":"46-commercial_building_transactive_control::v142-d-K008","paper":"46-commercial_building_transactive_control","label":"Occupancy-period enabling and five-minute update configuration for the two types of HVAC","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K008","label":"Occupancy-period enabling and five-minute update configuration for the two types of HVAC","market_meaning":"In the reported configuration, TC can be enabled only during occupied periods, the market period is five minutes, and the setpoint update interval of the building energy simulation is also five minutes; the occupancy condition is only a necessary condition for enabling.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M03","v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["coordination"],"scope_disposition":"compatible","scope_explanation":"R014 covers the reported configuration of the two HVAC types, and R002 retains the overlapping central-system statement within it. The market period and the simulation setpoint update interval are retained separately, are not merged because their values are the same, and are not generalized to the update period of all field devices.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"Occupancy status limits the enabling period, and the two time parameters limit market operation and simulation updates; these are independent operational configuration rules; the duplicated statement in the central chain is only a shared reference and does not increase the number of rules.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R014","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Primary responsibility for the enabling conditions and the two time parameters of the reported configuration for the two HVAC types."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"shared","role":"alternative","rationale":"Only the overlapping central-system configuration of C006 is retained as a narrower-scope representation, while the remaining coordination content is still primarily the responsibility of K004."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K008-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R014","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C006"],"evidence_ids":["ev-v141-b-g03-004","v141-b-g02-E034"],"rationale":"Both pieces of evidence explicitly report the configurations of the two systems, and the R002 frozen Rule-Chain is limited to the central system; therefore, within the overlapping central-system scope it corresponds to its configuration, while the broader system scope of R014 is retained."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K008-M01","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R014::theta::v141-c-R014-theta-market-period","v141-c-R002::theta::theta_market_period"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["ev-v141-b-g03-004","v141-b-g02-E034"],"rationale":"In the overlapping central-system configuration, both correspond to the same reported market period; R014 also covers RTU, so the source scope and local objects remain separate."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K008-M02","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R014::theta::v141-c-R014-theta-setpoint-update-interval","v141-c-R002::theta::theta_update_interval"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["ev-v141-b-g03-004","v141-b-g02-E034"],"rationale":"Within the overlapping central-system scope, both are the building-simulation setpoint update interval; they are not merged with the market-period object, nor extended to field-device sampling or execution periods."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K008-M03","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C006"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["ev-v141-b-g03-004","v141-b-g02-E034"],"rationale":"The two constraints describe broad and narrow scope representations of the same reported configuration, and R014 additionally expresses the occupancy necessary condition; their scopes of application differ, so they are not claimed to be fully duplicate constraints that can be deleted."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K008-G01","category":"unverified_source","description":"The occupancy condition and the five-minute parameters both come from unaudited candidate evidence; recognition of scope overlap does not mean that the configuration or equivalent translation has been independently verified.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R014","v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C006"],"evidence_ids":["ev-v141-b-g03-004","v141-b-g02-E034"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequently verify the original text of the reported configuration, and separately confirm the market period, simulation update interval, and occupancy condition; preserve the direction of the necessary condition and the scope of the worked example."}]},"rule_refs":["46-commercial_building_transactive_control::v141-c-R014","46-commercial_building_transactive_control::v141-c-R002"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-2922a59013d1b13e","COMP-5ec4be881f53e6e8","COMP-c08cf41f234ed625"]});
